  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I've personally had multiple instances of friends spamming invite requests which, while slightly annoying on its own, is made even worse due to the fact I then have to decline every single request after that to clear my inbox. I feel like it'd make more sense to just stack requests from the same user so we can mass decline in one press, or press accept on one and that gets rid of all the rest. What's really the point of interacting with more than one request from the same user, y'know?",
